# Entry Main: the contract of a structural call is the one its real parent describes (the book #structural-call,
# #return-in-data; step 21.7 K3). The root, the data of Main, and the sibling Q declare `return: int`; P, the parent of
# C, declares `return: @`: the call of C answers a reference. Were the contract taken from the data of the caller or from
# another Structure, the reference node\Box would be refused. The root place p is written and read by its explicit path
# (the book #binding-places). Box\v 5, a 5.
int: a 0
return: int
Q:
    return: int
P:
    Box:
        int: v 0
    end: Box
    return: @
    C:
        return: node\Box
    end: C
end: P
@: p 0
---
Main:
    node\p := P\C()
    node\p\v := 5
    node\a := node\p\v
